\chapter{ProgSnap2 Export and Analysis}
\label{progsnap2}

ProgSnap2 is a standardised data format for programming process
data, developed by the CS education community
(\url{https://cssplice.org/progsnap2/}).
It captures how students write code over time---exactly what
learnlog records---but in a format that analysis tools can consume
directly.

A ProgSnap2 dataset is a zip file containing:
\begin{description}
\item[DatasetMetadata.csv] Version and configuration fields.
\item[MainTable.csv] One row per event (file edits, program runs).
\item[CodeStates/] A directory of source file snapshots, one
  subdirectory per unique code state.
\item[Resources/] Individual I/O text files referenced by the
  [[ProgramOutput]] and [[ProgramInput]] columns.
\end{description}

We use the [[.progsnap2]] extension to distinguish these
files from Git bundles.

This chapter covers both \emph{writing} ProgSnap2 datasets
(the export pipeline) and \emph{reading} them back for
analysis.
The reading side parses a zip file into structured Python
data, can reconstruct a temporary Git repository for
[[play]]/[[list]], groups events into edit--run pairs,
and generates \LaTeX{} output that presents the student's
development process.


