The child events of the two kinds must also stay out of each other's
way, which is a property of the two rebuilders rather than of the
round trip, and is worth asking about directly.
The I/O event below carries a timestamp, which learnlog's own exporter
never gives one---that is the point.
Both rebuilders select their children by event type, and a test whose
I/O event had no timestamp would pass even if [[rebuild_view_trace]]
selected by nothing at all, because the missing timestamp would filter
it out by accident.
A dataset from a tool that does record per-line timing would then turn
every output chunk into a view of no commit.

