The awkward case is the one the export exists for: a [[python -c]] run,
whose first argument is a program source with spaces and newlines in
it, followed by the arguments the student actually passed.
Let's follow one all the way through---commit, export, read back---and
check that the list that comes out is the list that went in, while a
plain script run still reads like a command line in the column:

